WEBVTT

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:16.830
I can't do it now, but I won't give up

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.980
Because I've already woken up

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:25.050
The burning excitement reflects the times

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.770
My burning soul

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.500
No

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:02.660
We'll be right back.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:33.620
decision.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:35.810
No!

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:03.690
Lieutenant Emma's taking Unit 1.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.900
It's all right. Let her go.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.120
Stop me. I'm down.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:33.430
He's nuts! What's with this guy?

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:40.130
He's not killed my mother!

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:45.180
What are you talking about, Camille?

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:47.130
Jared, stop! Bite him!

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.110
It's just a kid pilot in Unit 3!

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.980
According to intelligence, the Aeyouk doesn't have any...

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:05.730
Isaks I don't think they do think isn't good enough do they or don't they they do not ma'am

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:58.170
Two boys, with the girl's name and me.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.480
Does this thing have any more?

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:03.070
Attack the AUC?

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:09.420
Are you friend or foe? What do you want?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:13.870
Stay back! I'm a Titan pilot. We don't need to start another battle.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:14.970
The enemy needs a little...

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.260
more time to think this over.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.730
Camille's lost it.

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:21.820
Poor kid.

00:05:30.316 --> 00:05:32.476
Are you saying we should give Bass what he wants?

00:05:32.908 --> 00:05:33.368
Yes.

00:05:33.804 --> 00:05:34.604
We can't.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:37.000
His forces are right on our heels.

00:05:37.836 --> 00:05:40.176
Lieutenant Air Machine doesn't intend to fight us.

00:05:40.276 --> 00:05:41.116
You're guessing.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.380
I know it.

00:05:43.148 --> 00:05:44.608
We can't trust the Titans.

00:05:44.888 --> 00:05:46.008
We can trust her.

00:05:46.348 --> 00:05:49.108
I have to say I agree with Lieutenant Quattro on this one.

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:49.848
Captain?

00:05:50.168 --> 00:05:50.868
Signing off.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.660
It could be executed if you don't obey the ceasefire.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:37.340
You have to calm down be quiet

00:06:37.996 --> 00:06:39.056
Get off of me!

00:06:39.156 --> 00:06:42.956
Camille Bidon, you have to swallow your emotions and act like a grown-up.

00:06:43.532 --> 00:06:44.132
But my mom!

00:06:44.428 --> 00:06:45.968
She was killed right in front of me!

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.160
Don't you know how I feel?

00:06:49.388 --> 00:06:49.888
Stop it!

00:06:49.932 --> 00:06:51.212
You're not helping things!

00:06:51.292 --> 00:06:51.852
I'm sorry.

00:06:52.072 --> 00:06:53.512
We're handing over the Mark Twos.

00:06:53.752 --> 00:06:54.252
You...

00:06:55.148 --> 00:06:56.428
Please follow up on it.

00:06:57.356 --> 00:06:59.276
You're Lieutenant Quattro Bagina, right?

00:06:59.660 --> 00:06:59.960
Are you?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.670
sure about this? Of course I'm sure. I gave the ceasefire signal, didn't I? I'm worried about how

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:10.260
Camille's doing. I'm going outside. I'll come with you. Let's go.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:29.690
Open the hide-in, it's Lieutenant Quatro!

00:07:30.156 --> 00:07:30.656
Ami-

00:07:35.916 --> 00:07:38.376
Looks like the Titans are getting their Gundams back.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:15.410
Well, the good news is that Camille's father, Franklin Bidon, is now safe.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.360
There's the possibility in the future we could bring him over to our side.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:20.500
Do you agree?

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.540
Oh, that's one way of looking at it.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:25.700
We made the right choice.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:26.600
What about Emma?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:27.800
Is she a new type?

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:29.740
I'm not really sure.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.100
She doesn't act like a titan officer.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:43.210
Captain, hmm?

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:45.920
With one move, our force has just doubled.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.290
We'll overwhelm the Argama.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.440
Sir, excellent idea.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:52.560
Still locked?

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.060
It's been locked from the inside.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.140
We're using a bypass code to open it.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:08:59.380
Should do it.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:02.810
So, we finally meet face-to-face, Camille.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:06.290
Come on, kid.

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:08.340
Was Lieutenant Hilda really in there?

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:14.020
Was she in it?

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.230
Of course she was!

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:18.130
It wasn't a trick or a hologram?

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:20.350
Unit 3's fingers will prove it.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:21.280
Fingers?

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:37.720
Get out!

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:45.410
I don't need your-

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:45.690
Camille!

00:09:58.020 --> 00:09:58.520
What is it?

00:09:59.340 --> 00:09:59.520
Dad.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:02.220
Mom's dead.

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:07.020
The Titans shot her in cold blood.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.620
I saw it with my own eyes.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.170
How did this happen?

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.660
Didn't you know that you and Mom were hostages?

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:18.920
Camille!

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.900
Looks like it's just you and your mistress now.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:23.820
It's Margarita, right?

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:24.420
Stop!

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.320
The truth, isn't it?

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:29.980
Camille, why did your mother have...

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:36.320
to die tell me I don't know I I was just trying to save her dad but the people

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:40.380
responsible for her death are the ones on this ship they put her out there

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:52.160
mistress you're saying Captain Bask is behind this wouldn't you say that this

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.040
was good news for you and Margarita

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:06.920
So, that was your mom, hey?

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:08.840
For what it's worth, I'm sorry.

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:11.790
I honestly had no idea she was in that capsule.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:16.600
And it must be hard seeing as how you're a baby.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:17.340
Tragic.

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:20.240
You can take a swing at me if you want,

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:22.500
like you did at the spaceport that time.

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:26.530
Now I see.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.970
You were just carrying out your order.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.860
A soldier has to obey a superior's command.

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:36.440
Even if you're stupid, you're just doing your duty.

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:38.820
I forgive you.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:42.470
I'm good enough to beat you and the highs, AccuPilot.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:45.220
But I'm powerless before the system.

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:47.340
Cruel military system.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:51.300
And its cruelty breeds the worst hatred.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:53.640
I'm back here, you little...

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:54.300
Jared, stop!

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:55.740
This fight is over.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:57.580
Like a Titan officer.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.980
Show a little control and move on, will you?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:15.210
I've been thinking.

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:15.790
Sir?

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:19.180
I don't want to use hostages if I can help it.

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:22.490
On the next mission, I want you to show me how you'd handle it.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.380
How I'd handle it?

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:25.300
That is correct.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:29.550
I want you to capture one of the Argama's new mobile suits without trickery.

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:35.870
I believe you can do this, because you're actually brave enough to disagree with me.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:37.490
But, sir...

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:39.550
Don't worry, you won't be alone.

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:42.660
I'll allow you to team up with Lila's unit for this operation.

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:47.130
You're also free to use the three Gundam Mark IIs.

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:54.760
If it pleases you, sir, I'd like to pilot one of those Gundam Mark IIs to make up for my disgrace.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.400
Make up for it?

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:59.970
You have to prove yourself before you can worry about your...

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:03.300
Lieutenant, you make the choice.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:14.000
I have a feeling that Lieutenant Emma will be returning here quite soon.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:17.740
The Commodore doesn't think so, but we'll remain in the area just the same.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.260
Personally, I'd like to see Lieutenant Emma again.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:23.200
Yes, so would I.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:39.550
I made a gun to Mark II.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:43.460
Of course, considering I was the one who designed it.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:46.590
Please accept my condolences on the loss of your wife.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:48.180
Thank you.

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:52.260
I'm leaving, and I've come here to find out if you want to go with me.

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:56.530
Deserting? You're going to the Argama, I take it?

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:57.010
Yes.

00:13:57.530 --> 00:13:58.410
And if I refuse?

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:03.170
I understand. Let's go.

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:14.350
Decided to leave the Alexandria. Do you have the courage to come?

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:15.410
With you?

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:17.790
That's right. Do you have the courage?

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:21.380
Sure I do. If you're telling the truth.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:22.320
Of course I am.

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:29.860
I'm not a child. I'll follow you.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:30.870
Sorry.

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:38.020
My dad's coming, too?

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:38.990
Why not?

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:42.400
Listen carefully.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:45.260
We're like prisoners when we get to the normal suit room.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:45.820
Right.

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:50.340
I'd like to know what you're thinking about, Dad.

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:59.550
Keep your shirt on, just because you're team leader.

00:14:59.850 --> 00:14:59.970
Her!

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:02.250
What's going on?

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:03.090
Beats me.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:03.870
Captain's orders.

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:18.930
We better hurry.

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:22.430
Good work.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.200
Where did you put my normal suit?

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:25.980
You can't wear their uniform here.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:27.160
We'll find you a new one.

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:29.970
Camille, you have...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.820
You haven't had a chance to pilot the AUG's new mobile suit yet, have you?

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:37.640
Chit-chat can wait till we're out of here.

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:40.090
Let's get this straight.

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:43.000
I'm not doing this because I feel sorry for you two.

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:45.170
I'm doing this for myself.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.020
Is that clear?

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:48.060
Perfectly.

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:50.940
Lieutenant, straighten your back like a pilot would.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:51.490
Please.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:53.040
Looking good.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:55.660
Don't look so sad.

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:56.970
Maybe next time.

00:15:58.800 --> 00:15:59.940
So, how does it feel?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:06.650
to lead a team into battle. Nervous? Feels pretty good. I imagine it would. She's now leading

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:15.540
Kakrikon and Lieutenant Deva Barrow. He might need some advice. Just a minute, Kakrikon.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:19.780
This is the best combat mission of the Gundam Mark 2s. Double check everything, people. We

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:22.900
don't want anything to go wrong on this mission. We're leading it at once, so take it easy.

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:28.060
The Argama is the type of ship that... Hey! Kakrikon! What's the big deal?

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:29.960
Ella! What are you doing?

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:31.380
It's too early.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:34.890
Doors aren't even open yet.

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:36.290
Something's wrong.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:39.750
All three of them?

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:40.880
Lieutenant Emma?

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:42.110
Lieutenant Emma!

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:47.760
What's she thinking?

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:49.300
Is she nuts?

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:52.280
Anyone not wearing a normal suit should get to an airlock.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:02.680
Lieutenant Franklin, report.

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:03.880
Uh, the system's okay.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:04.600
And Camille?

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:05.060
Ready.

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:10.720
Proceed, yeah, Lieutenant!

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:13.450
Listen, Controller, it's not Catricon.

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:14.190
Stop them!

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:14.670
Huh?

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:16.610
Now what?

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:22.380
Use the beam rifle.

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:22.860
No!

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:26.080
What was that tremor I just felt?

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.890
Apparently, Lieutenant Emma is stealing the Gundams.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:29.730
Stealing them?

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.300
And the other pilots?

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:36.200
Close. Just follow me.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:37.820
Got it. Right behind you.

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:38.580
Launching.

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:47.070
Launching.

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:53.260
Nice one. I'm impressed.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.080
All right, let's do it.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:10.310
want an explanation. Is she acting alone? No, sir. She's taking Camille and Franklin Bidan

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:16.420
with her as well. Lieutenant Franklin? So he is a traitor.

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:34.450
Why didn't you dodge it, Dad?

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:45.590
Getcha.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:52.890
Only one thruster was damaged.

00:18:53.180 --> 00:18:54.980
That shouldn't prevent me from flying.

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:56.760
I designed it to work that way.

00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:59.830
Are you sure you're able to follow me?

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:04.870
but at a reduced speed are they kidding they're gonna catch us at this speed

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:13.930
here's one already Camille unit 2 is setting the course don't wander or we'll

00:19:13.930 --> 00:19:20.680
lose you Roger so and the Gundams are all together

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:51.540
always gets in the way it hit it shots in your energy pack use them carefully roger that

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:58.380
quattro's hunch was right measure the distance to those flashes is it true i heard the mark twos

00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.800
are returning nothing's confirmed

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.340
But it looks that way.

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:02.420
Let's hope so.

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:03.630
Where's Quattro?

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:22.440
Fire that rifle.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.490
You designed this mobile suit, right?

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:27.240
Uh, I'll try using the Vulcans.

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:29.960
Unit 3.

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:39.930
Where are forcements?

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:54.590
He's searching.

00:20:56.930 --> 00:20:57.330
Get away.

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:02.640
We have three Gundam Mark IIs.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:04.960
Who's piloting them?

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:08.130
That looks like Lieutenant Quattro's suit.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:10.720
An AU mobile suit.

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:17.120
Welcome back.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:18.860
Thanks to Emma.

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:24.140
Emma Sheen.

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:27.600
Lieutenant Quattro Begina.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.880
Lieutenant, forgive.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:35.430
me, but I'm finding it hard to believe in your change of heart. The Titans are an elite group,

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:45.070
after all. That's all right. I understand. What happened with the Titans? Or maybe you just

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:51.870
changed? It's just that I always try to follow the path I believe in. That hasn't changed at all.

00:21:52.860 --> 00:21:55.330
That's right. Emma is a good person.

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:06.540
Lieutenant Franklin.

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:13.340
Dad? Dad!

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:17.290
This is a very well-designed mobile suit.

00:22:23.180 --> 00:22:26.250
Selfish. He's always off in his own world.

00:23:31.980 --> 00:23:48.920
and sons rarely see eye to eye.

00:23:49.440 --> 00:23:51.040
Camille has a hard time understanding

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:53.640
why Franklin would take Char's Rick Diaz

00:23:53.640 --> 00:23:55.040
and escape from the Argama.

00:23:55.550 --> 00:23:57.830
His father is the only family left to him.

00:23:58.070 --> 00:23:59.970
But all Camille can do is watch him.

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:02.770
as he floats away into the depths of outer space.

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:08.520
Stun Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam, father and son.

00:24:08.890 --> 00:24:10.870
You will see the tears of time.
